---
import ClusterMap from './ClusterMap.astro';
import { actors, flows, faults, gatePresets, type View } from './api-server-data';
interface Props { view: View; }
const { view } = Astro.props;
const capabilities = [
  { group:'Fundamental', items:[['Versioned API and discovery','Clients discover groups such as /api/v1 and /apis/apps/v1 before working with objects.'],['Defaulting, conversion and validation','A versioned request becomes a valid object before accepted state is stored.']] },
  { group:'Security', items:[['Authentication and authorization','The API identifies a caller and checks the requested verb, resource and scope.'],['Admission and webhooks','Applicable writes can be mutated or denied; a matched webhook is an API-server-initiated call.']] },
  { group:'State', items:[['Storage interface and etcd','Durable backing state sits behind API serving; ordinary Kubernetes clients do not use etcd as their API.'],['LIST/WATCH and watch cache','Clients follow changes through API watches; serving caches mean every read is not a physical etcd request.']] },
  { group:'Performance', items:[['API Priority and Fairness','Requests can be classified into priority levels and queued or rejected under pressure.']] },
  { group:'Extensibility', items:[['Aggregation and APIService','Registered extension API paths can be proxied to an aggregated server.'],['Subresources','/status, /scale, /log, /exec and /portforward have distinct purposes and authorization.']] },
  { group:'Operations', items:[['Audit trail','Request stages can generate policy-controlled audit records.'],['Control-plane-to-node proxy','Pod logs, attach and port-forward use special API-server-to-kubelet paths.']] },
];
---
<ClusterMap mapId={view.id} depth={view.id==='responsibilities'||view.id==='conversations'||view.id==='failures'||view.id==='ha-state'?'internals':view.id==='control-data'?'practitioner':'foundation'} />

{view.id==='exchange' && <div class="api-view-fixture"><strong>Start with kubectl. Then inspect another client.</strong><p>Try controller manager, scheduler, kubelet or an extension. Each uses the API for the state it owns; etcd remains behind the API server.</p><div class="api-myth-line"><span>LIKELY MODEL</span><del>kubectl → etcd or controller → kubelet</del><span>ACTUAL MODEL</span><strong>client / controller / kubelet ↔ Kubernetes API state</strong></div></div>}

{view.id==='request-gates' && <div class="api-gate-lab" data-api-gate-lab>
  <div class="api-gate-head"><div role="group" aria-label="API request type"><button type="button" data-gate-mode="write" aria-pressed="true">WRITE · CREATE</button><button type="button" data-gate-mode="read" aria-pressed="false">READ · GET/LIST/WATCH</button></div><label>Inject a failure <select data-gate-preset>{gatePresets.map((preset)=><option value={preset.id}>{preset.label}</option>)}</select></label></div>
  <ol class="api-gate-rail" data-gate-rail><li data-gate="0"><strong>01</strong><span>TLS / API route</span><small>REQUEST</small></li><li data-gate="1"><strong>02</strong><span>Authentication</span><small>WHO?</small></li><li data-gate="2"><strong>03</strong><span>Authorization</span><small>MAY?</small></li><li data-gate="3"><strong>04</strong><span>Mutating admission</span><small>CHANGE?</small></li><li data-gate="4"><strong>05</strong><span>Validating admission</span><small>ALLOW?</small></li><li data-gate="5"><strong>06</strong><span>Resource processing</span><small>VALID?</small></li><li data-gate="6"><strong>07</strong><span>Persistence</span><small>COMMIT</small></li></ol>
  <div class="api-gate-result" data-gate-result aria-live="polite"><strong>WRITE REQUEST · STEP 1</strong><p>Request enters the API route. No Deployment is stored yet.</p></div><div class="api-lab-controls"><button type="button" data-gate-reset>Reset</button><button type="button" data-gate-prev aria-label="Previous request gate">← Gate</button><button type="button" data-gate-play>▶ Play gates</button><button type="button" data-gate-next aria-label="Next request gate">Gate →</button></div><p class="api-context-note">Teaching pipeline: authentication → authorization → applicable admission → persistence. Ordinary reads bypass admission; a rejected write never reaches etcd.</p>
</div>}

{view.id==='watch' && <div class="api-watch-lab" data-api-watch-lab><div class="watch-before"><span>NAIVE POLLING MODEL</span><del>Controller asks again and again: “anything changed?”</del></div><ol class="api-watch-rail"><li data-watch-step="0"><strong>01 LIST</strong><span>Deployment/demo/web · resourceVersion 10245</span></li><li data-watch-step="1"><strong>02 WATCH</strong><span>Keep a change stream from that version</span></li><li data-watch-step="2"><strong>03 EVENT</strong><span>MODIFIED · resourceVersion 11020</span></li><li data-watch-step="3"><strong>04 RECONCILE</strong><span>Queue demo/web · compare desired with observed</span></li></ol><div class="api-lab-controls"><button type="button" data-watch-prev>← Previous</button><button type="button" data-watch-next>Next →</button><button type="button" data-watch-reset>Reset watch</button></div><details><summary>Show client internals</summary><p>Reflector → local informer cache → handlers → work queue → Reconcile(). The cache can be temporarily behind API state; a logical decision need not issue another GET.</p></details><details><summary>Show server internals</summary><p>API handlers, watch cache and storage interface sit behind the served API. A WATCH event should not be drawn as a separate physical etcd request every time.</p></details><p class="api-context-note">If historical changes are unavailable, `410 Gone` tells a client to clear/re-LIST and restart its watch.</p></div>}

{view.id==='spec-status' && <div class="api-state-lab" data-api-state-lab><div class="api-state-bars"><div><span>SPEC · DESIRED</span><strong>3 replicas</strong><meter min="0" max="3" value="3">3 of 3</meter></div><div><span>STATUS · READY</span><strong data-state-ready>0 replicas</strong><meter data-state-meter min="0" max="3" value="0">0 of 3</meter></div></div><div class="api-reconcile-rail"><span>OBSERVE</span><span>COMPARE 3 − READY</span><span>ACT THROUGH API</span><span>↺ OBSERVE AGAIN</span></div><div class="api-version-choices" role="group" aria-label="Inspect web-a object version"><button type="button" data-pod-version="unscheduled" aria-pressed="true">Before binding</button><button type="button" data-pod-version="bound" aria-pressed="false">Bound</button><button type="button" data-pod-version="running" aria-pressed="false">Running and Ready</button></div><pre data-pod-yaml>{'kind: Pod\nmetadata: {name: web-a}\nspec: {nodeName: null}\nstatus: {phase: Pending}'}</pre><p data-pod-version-result aria-live="polite">The Pod exists as API state; scheduler has not recorded placement and kubelet has not started a container.</p></div>}

{view.id==='flow-lab' && <div class="api-flow-lab" data-api-flow-lab><div class="api-flow-head"><label>Choose a cluster conversation <select data-flow-select>{(['foundation','practitioner','internals'] as const).map((tier)=><optgroup label={tier==='foundation'?'Foundation':tier==='practitioner'?'Practitioner':'Internals'}>{flows.filter((flow)=>flow.group===tier).map((flow)=><option value={flow.id}>{flow.title}</option>)}</optgroup>)}</select></label><div class="api-flow-focus"><strong data-flow-title>Create a Deployment</strong><p data-flow-question>Does applying replicas: 3 mean three containers exist already?</p></div></div><ol class="api-flow-timeline" data-flow-timeline aria-label="Selected flow steps">{flows[0].steps.map((step,i)=><li><button type="button" data-flow-step={i} aria-current={i===0?'step':undefined}><span>{String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span>{step.label}</button></li>)}</ol><div class="api-lab-controls"><button type="button" data-flow-first title="First step">|←</button><button type="button" data-flow-prev title="Previous step">←</button><button type="button" data-flow-play>▶ Play Deployment</button><button type="button" data-flow-next title="Next step">→</button><button type="button" data-flow-last title="Final step">→|</button><label>Speed <select data-flow-speed><option value="2">0.5×</option><option value="1" selected>1×</option><option value="0.5">2×</option></select></label><button type="button" data-flow-reset>Reset</button></div><div class="api-flow-step-summary" data-flow-summary aria-live="polite"><strong>01 · Apply</strong><p>Alice sends desired replicas: 3 through the Kubernetes API.</p></div><details><summary>Show API operation and object fields</summary><div><code data-flow-operation>CREATE Deployment</code><pre data-flow-yaml>{flows[0].steps[0].yaml}</pre></div></details><p class="api-context-note">All 23 scenarios share the topology above. Select another flow and the actors stay put while the selected operation and object state change.</p><div class="api-flow-static" aria-label="All flow reading paths without JavaScript"><h3>All cluster conversations</h3>{flows.map((flow,i)=><details><summary>{String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')} · {flow.title}</summary><p>{flow.question} {flow.takeaway}</p><ol>{flow.steps.map((step)=><li><strong>{step.label} · {step.operation}</strong> — {step.detail}</li>)}</ol><p>{flow.caveat}</p><p>{flow.sources.map((url)=><a href={url}>Primary reference ↗ </a>)}</p></details>)}</div></div>}

{view.id==='conversations' && <div class="api-conversation-lab"><div class="api-map-filters" role="group" aria-label="Filter the cluster map"><strong>FILTER ACTORS</strong>{[['humans','Humans'],['control','Control plane'],['nodes','Nodes'],['networking','Networking'],['storage','Storage'],['autoscaling','Autoscaling'],['extensions','Extensions'],['external','External']].map(([id,label])=><button type="button" data-map-filter={id} aria-pressed="false">{label}</button>)}<button type="button" data-map-filter="all" aria-pressed="true">All</button></div><div class="api-actor-shortlist"><strong>Try a component</strong>{actors.filter((actor)=>['api','controller','scheduler','node-a','proxy','csi','cloud','operator'].includes(actor.id)).map((actor)=><button type="button" data-actor-shortcut={actor.id}>{actor.label}</button>)}</div><p>The controller manager hosts multiple loops: Deployment, ReplicaSet, Node lifecycle, EndpointSlice, HPA and others. A kubelet’s primary scope is its own Node.</p><details><summary>Read the component relationship inventory</summary><dl>{actors.map((actor)=><div><dt>{actor.label}</dt><dd><strong>READS:</strong> {actor.reads}. <strong>WATCHES:</strong> {actor.watches}. <strong>WRITES:</strong> {actor.writes}. <strong>WHY:</strong> {actor.why}.</dd></div>)}</dl></details></div>}

{view.id==='control-data' && <div class="api-dataplane-lab" data-api-dataplane-lab><fieldset><legend>Highlight a path</legend><label><input type="radio" name="api-plane" value="control" checked />Control plane</label><label><input type="radio" name="api-plane" value="data" />Data plane</label><label><input type="radio" name="api-plane" value="both" />Both</label></fieldset><div class="api-plane-rails"><div><span>CONTROL STATE</span><strong>EndpointSlice controller → API → Service proxy</strong><small>WATCH / CREATE EndpointSlice · app=web</small></div><div><span>APPLICATION DATA</span><strong>Client HTTP → Service forwarding → web Pod</strong><small>No ordinary HTTP hop through kube-apiserver</small></div></div><p data-plane-result aria-live="polite">Control-plane API state tells a node dataplane which backend addresses are eligible.</p></div>}

{view.id==='failures' && <div class="api-failure-lab" data-api-failure-lab><label>Fail one component or dependency <select data-fault-select>{faults.map((fault)=><option value={fault.id}>{fault.label}</option>)}</select></label><ol class="api-fault-timeline" data-fault-timeline>{faults[0].steps.map((step,i)=><li><button type="button" data-fault-step={i} aria-current={i===0?'step':undefined}><span>{String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span>{step.label}</button></li>)}</ol><div class="api-lab-controls"><button type="button" data-fault-first>|←</button><button type="button" data-fault-prev>← Previous</button><button type="button" data-fault-play>▶ Play fault</button><button type="button" data-fault-next>Next →</button><button type="button" data-fault-reset>Reset fault</button></div><div class="api-fault-outcome" aria-live="polite"><strong data-fault-title>Kill one Pod</strong><dl><div><dt>STOPS</dt><dd data-fault-field="stops">{faults[0].stops}</dd></div><div><dt>CONTINUES</dt><dd data-fault-field="continues">{faults[0].continues}</dd></div><div><dt>FIRST DETECTOR</dt><dd data-fault-field="detector">{faults[0].detector}</dd></div><div><dt>API OBJECT CHANGE</dt><dd data-fault-field="object">{faults[0].object}</dd></div><div><dt>REACTING LOOP</dt><dd data-fault-field="reactor">{faults[0].reactor}</dd></div><div><dt>WORKLOAD TRAFFIC</dt><dd data-fault-field="traffic">{faults[0].traffic}</dd></div><div><dt>RECOVERY CONDITION</dt><dd data-fault-field="recovery">{faults[0].recovery}</dd></div></dl></div><p data-fault-summary aria-live="polite">Pod B exits: observed readiness falls to two while desired replicas stay three.</p><details class="api-fault-static"><summary>Read all failure outcomes</summary>{faults.map((fault)=><div><h3>{fault.label}</h3><p><strong>Stops:</strong> {fault.stops}. <strong>Continues:</strong> {fault.continues}. <strong>Detector:</strong> {fault.detector}. <strong>API object:</strong> {fault.object}. <strong>Reactor:</strong> {fault.reactor}. <strong>Traffic:</strong> {fault.traffic}. <strong>Recovery:</strong> {fault.recovery}.</p></div>)}</details></div>}

{view.id==='ha-state' && <div class="api-ha-lab" data-api-ha-lab><div class="api-ha-route"><span>CONTROL-PLANE ENDPOINT</span><strong>Load balancer / VIP</strong><span>↓ ROUTE TO SERVING REPLICA</span><div><b data-ha-replica="1">API1 · SERVING</b><b data-ha-replica="2">API2 · SERVING</b><b data-ha-replica="3">API3 · SERVING</b></div><span>↓ DURABLE BACKING</span><strong data-ha-etcd>etcd · HEALTHY</strong></div><div class="api-ha-choices" role="group" aria-label="API high availability state"><button type="button" data-ha-choice="healthy" aria-pressed="true">All healthy</button><button type="button" data-ha-choice="replica" aria-pressed="false">Fail API2</button><button type="button" data-ha-choice="endpoint" aria-pressed="false">Fail endpoint</button><button type="button" data-ha-choice="etcd" aria-pressed="false">Degrade etcd</button></div><p data-ha-result aria-live="polite">API1, API2 and API3 can serve requests concurrently. Controller-manager and scheduler leader election use separate Leases.</p><div class="api-lease-note"><strong>SEPARATE LEASE COORDINATION</strong><span>Controller-manager A active · B standby</span><span>Scheduler A active · B standby</span><span>Node Lease renewals report liveness, not API-server serving leadership.</span></div></div>}

{view.id==='responsibilities' && <div class="api-responsibility-lab"><div class="api-capability-list">{capabilities.map((category,categoryIndex)=><details open={categoryIndex===0}><summary>{category.group}</summary><div>{category.items.map(([title,copy])=><button type="button" data-capability-title={title} data-capability-copy={copy}>{title}</button>)}</div></details>)}</div><div class="api-capability-inspector" aria-live="polite"><strong data-capability-active>Versioned API and discovery</strong><p data-capability-description>Clients discover groups such as /api/v1 and /apis/apps/v1 before working with objects.</p><pre>{'/api/v1\n/apis/apps/v1\n/apis/metrics.k8s.io/v1beta1\n/apis/example.io/v1'}</pre></div><details><summary>Show direct-call exceptions</summary><ul><li>API server → kubelet: Pod logs, attach and port-forward.</li><li>API server → matched admission/authentication/authorization webhook.</li><li>API server → aggregated API server for registered extension paths.</li><li>Cloud, CSI, Gateway and Operator controllers → external providers where configured.</li></ul></details></div>}

{view.id==='one-picture' && <div class="api-finale-lab" data-api-finale-lab><div class="api-finale-model"><div><span>HYPOTHETICAL DIRECT COUPLING</span><del>controller ↔ scheduler ↔ kubelet ↔ etcd ↔ every extension</del><small>Not normal Kubernetes state coordination</small></div><div><span>API-CENTERED COORDINATION</span><strong>INTENT → API STATE → LOOPS → NODE REALITY → STATUS ↺</strong><small>Shared objects, policy, watches and independent scope</small></div></div><button type="button" data-finale-step>Reveal the repeated pattern</button><p data-finale-result aria-live="polite">Kubernetes is a distributed system of reconciliation loops centered around a shared, versioned API.</p><details><summary>Show API objects</summary><p>Deployments · ReplicaSets · Pods · Nodes · Leases · Services · EndpointSlices · Secrets · ConfigMaps · PVCs · PVs · HPAs · RoleBindings · CRDs · custom resources.</p></details><details><summary>Check the seven tempting shortcuts</summary><ul class="api-misconceptions"><li><strong>kubectl is Kubernetes.</strong><span>kubectl is one API client.</span></li><li><strong>Scheduler starts Pods.</strong><span>Scheduler records placement; kubelet executes assigned PodSpecs.</span></li><li><strong>Controllers command kubelets.</strong><span>They normally coordinate indirectly through API state.</span></li><li><strong>Every component uses etcd directly.</strong><span>Ordinary Kubernetes clients use the API server.</span></li><li><strong>WATCH means continuous etcd polling.</strong><span>API watches plus server and client caches form a reactive path.</span></li><li><strong>All network traffic uses kube-apiserver.</strong><span>Ordinary workload traffic follows the data plane.</span></li><li><strong>An API outage instantly kills running containers.</strong><span>Existing node workloads can continue while coordination is impaired.</span></li></ul></details><div class="api-operational-loop"><strong>WHEN THE CLUSTER STALLS</strong><ol><li>Check API endpoint availability, latency and audit evidence.</li><li>Compare object spec with status and the last changed resourceVersion.</li><li>Inspect controller progress, pending scheduling and Node/Lease freshness.</li><li>Check runtime, Service dataplane and storage separately from API state.</li><li>Rehearse recovery of the first broken dependency, then watch loops converge.</li></ol></div></div>}
